#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Wave 42: Just Teens, a Fourth Time — the floor rises to eight.

Wave 41 closed by naming this wave: the 13/14 band was still
the thinnest in the vault at 104 against 160 at the young
end, its floor was 7, and stem was the tie's other half at 9.
This wave's fresh audit measured the whole archive again
before anything was built. Per-age coverage at wave 41's
close: 3: 160, 4: 160, 5: 329, 6: 426, 7: 496, 8: 530,
9: 524, 10: 518, 11: 456, 12: 446, 13: 104, 14: 104.
Inside the band, the primary-category cells measure
seasons 7, outdoor 7, pe-movement 7, music-rhythm 7,
rainy-day 7, icebreakers 8, crafts 8, stem 9, holidays 10,
quiet-focus 15, team-community 19 — a floor of 7, shared
by five categories.

The wave's size is sized from those cells, the same way
waves 39, 40 and 41 sized theirs: the eight thinnest cells
in the band are the five at the floor of 7, the two at 8,
and stem at 9. One record for each of those eight cells is
eight records — no more, no fewer. Result, asserted in the
wave log: total 731 -> 739; age-13 coverage 104 -> 112 and
age-14 coverage 104 -> 112, every other age unchanged; the
13/14 primary floor rises 7 -> 8 (every category in the
band now carries at least 8 primaries); 13-14-only records
28 -> 36; and eight honest picks meet the build validator's
8-12 collection rule, so the 31st collection — "Just
Teens, a Fourth Time" — unlocks at exactly the 8-pick
minimum with no padding and no lowered bar. The remaining
gap to the 160 benchmark is 48 at each age, stated
numerically, not spun.

Deliberate neighbours, kept on purpose and named here:
- overwintering-garlic-planting-crew vs seed-starting-cups
  (sowing in spring for a quick start) and cold-
  stratification-seed-bank (wave 41, seed given a logged
  winter in jars): the garlic crew plants REAL CLOVES in
  real ground in autumn, mulches them against the winter,
  and counts spring emergence shoot by shoot — a crop
  whose whole timetable is the season itself.
- dusk-bat-exit-count vs star-party-hosts (wave 40, teens
  host families under a night sky) and bird-call-count
  (5-14, calls counted in daylight silence): the count
  tallies BATS leaving a known roost at dusk, in sectors,
  by the minute, from one set watch point — the animals
  are the event, the sky is only the light they leave by.
- tchoukball-first-session vs referee-run-round-robin
  (wave 39, teens officiate a tournament) and frisbee-
  golf-nine (a disc thrown at targets): tchoukball is a
  live team invasion game with no contact and no goal —
  shots rebound off a frame and the CATCH is the defence.
- song-arranging-studio-first-session vs parody-songs
  (new comic words to a known tune) and part-singing-
  choir-first-rehearsals (wave 41, voices holding parts):
  the studio keeps the song and changes its SKELETON —
  tempo, meter, order and instrumentation — and rehearses
  the arrangement as a argued, logged version.
- one-room-documentary-crew vs mini-podcast-studio
  (12-14, a spoken podcast) and photo-story-sequence
  (still images sequenced): the crew shoots a real short
  DOCUMENTARY film about one room — consent first, a shot
  plan before any camera rolls, interviews on the record.
- spectrum-line-introductions vs would-you-rather-circle
  (choices talked from chairs) and partner-portrait-
  interviews (wave 41, one deep pair interview): the line
  answers with FEET first — a whole room physically sorts
  itself along a line, then talks across the distance.
- pamphlet-stitch-bookbinding-studio vs one-sheet-zine-
  workshop (wave 41, a publication folded from one sheet)
  and commonplace-book-first-pages (wave 39, writing in a
  book): the studio BINDS the book itself — signatures,
  a stitched spine, covers cut true — before a word in it.
- solar-oven-temperature-trials vs wind-turbine-blade-
  trials (wave 39, one variable at a time against wind)
  and shadow-clock-sundial (telling time by shadow): the
  ovens cook by SUNLIGHT alone and are graded by a
  temperature log kept by the minute — heat, not time
  and not lift, is the measure.

Two drafted records were cut before the pack ran, on the
standing near-dupe discipline: a guided constellation
tour for the outdoor slot — star-party-hosts (wave 40)
already hosts a night-sky tour rehearsed from that
night's chart, and older guides do not make it a new
record — and a speed-introductions carousel for the
icebreakers slot — two-minute-mingle already runs many
short chats against a clock, and faster chairs do not
make it a new record. Both slots were rebuilt from
genuinely empty ground: no bat-exit count and no spectrum
line existed anywhere on the shelf.

The drama/coding lane, recorded not padded (standing
rule): still no drama or coding category among the
eleven, and no validator tag names one. The one-room
documentary is filed under rainy-day, its honest primary;
this wave does not invent a twelfth category to look
complete, and it does not bolt a coding record onto the
STEM slot to look complete either — the solar trials earn
that slot on heat and data, the archive's own terms.

Safety notes are practical only — no medical claims anywhere.

Run once: dedupes by id, writes data/activities.json and
data/collections.json. Run scripts/build.py afterwards.
"""
